{"event_id": "evt_0015", "session": 1, "turn_no": 1, "world_time": "Sandbox B, night", "actor": "gm", "kind": "gm_narration", "summary": "Narration for amw8frqnmasriim.", "visibility": "player", "knowledge_type": "fact", "known_to": [], "caused_by": [], "roll_ids": [], "tags": [], "details": {"text": "You slide the blaster into its holster and cross the thirty-five feet to the cart, Wick's lantern bobbing at your shoulder.\n\nUp close it is what it looked like: a cutting torch on a long hose, coupled to two gas bottles as tall as your waist, strapped upright. The gauges sit at part-full. You haul the straps tight until the bottles stop rocking, then close your left hand on the cart's bar. It rolls when you lean on it.\n\nWick touches your sleeve and points.\n\nDown the lane, at the Grange, a door has opened and closed. A lamp is coming up toward the silos, swinging at a walking pace, maybe a hundred and eighty feet away. You can't see who carries it. Your blade is the brightest thing on the rise.\n\nThe shed is thirty-five feet back. The cart is in your hand. What do you do?\n"}, "idempotency_key": "amw8frqnmasriim:narr"}
